1
00:00:01,890 --> 00:00:08,220
ImmD is how close, in pips, a pending order must be to the market before Orders marks it imminent.

2
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:12,590
By default it is the server's value. To use your own for this instrument, untick Default.

3
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:21,180
Type the distance and click OK. It changes what you see, not the clients' orders.

4
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:25,340
In Orders, an order within that distance of the market has a light amber row.

5
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,700
This one is farther away, so it is not marked.

6
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:33,990
These two orders are linked as OCO: each shows its partner.

7
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:40,240
Link this order to one of them with Link OCO Order.

8
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:49,420
That order is already linked, so you are asked first. Replace moves the link.

9
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:59,990
The stop order is now linked to the new one, and the first order is left unlinked.

10
00:01:00,090 --> 00:01:05,140
To go back to the server's value, tick Default and click OK.

11
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:07,640
ImmD shows the server's value again.

